# React Standards

## Component Organization
- Group by feature: Place related components in a folder if there are several for a feature
- UI primitives: Place generic, reusable UI components in the `ui/` folder

## Code Patterns
- Always use early return for conditional if relevant
- When moving logic from component to another, remove the old one

## Component Structure
- Use functional components
- Keep components light and small
- Strongly type `props`
- One component per file (except tiny private components)

## State Management
- Delegate state and logic to a smart component
- Return `null` if mandatory props are missing

## Style and Accessibility
- Think mobile-first
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Add appropriate ARIA attributes
- Ensure keyboard navigation
